required":false,"type":"array","values":[]},"title":{"acyclic":null,"additional_properties":false,"entity":null,"inverse":null,"items":null,"max":null,"max_length":null,"min":null,"min_length":null,"properties":{},"required":false,"type":"string","values":[]},"withholds":{"acyclic":null,"additional_properties":false,"entity":null,"inverse":null,"items":null,"max":null,"max_length":null,"min":null,"min_length":null,"properties":{},"required":false,"type":"string","values":[]}}},"version":1},"entity":"story","events":[],"from_state":"active","id":"ent-618aae4276b6ecbd6ebdcd9c9469ec56","result":{"entity":"story","fields":{"body":"## Outcome\n\n`eventlog_tree::copy` linearizes an `eventlog-tree` store into a SQLite store: groups in the tree's\nposition order, each stream gapless, and every event's original `{version, digest, parents}` kept\nin an origin table beside the events, so redaction cannot erase it. A refused copy writes nothing.\n\nDesign: aep `docs/design/planning-on-entity-runtime-v0.1.md` § 9.6, unit V3 (`copy`; `verify` and\n`repair` shipped in 0.4.0).\n\n## Decisions\n\n- A library function, not a CLI: this repository has no CLI crate.\n- Origins live in `<prefix>_origins`, written in the event's own transaction through\n  `RestoredEvent.origin`, and created on the first append that carries one, so an owner opened\n  with `open_existing` gains it without that function creating tables.\n- Everything the target's state can decide is checked before the first write: existing events, a\n  different stream identity (read with the new non-minting `stored_stream_identity`), a blob\n  digest bound to other bytes, restored identities already queued.\n- A refused restored append puts back every restored identity it took.\n\n## Not done\n\n- Tenant capture does not carry origins (`TenantCapture` is a core type built in 14 places).\n- Postgres: no origin table and no copy; the design defers it.\n\n## Review\n\nAdversary pass 1 returned NEEDS-CHANGE (an owner without the origin table, the restored queue on\nrefusal, a partial write on a late refusal); all three are fixed and pinned by its tests.\n","document":{"events":[{"args":{"command":"move-status","decided_on":"{\"recorded\":{\"test_result\":1}}","target":"ent-618aae4276b6ecbd6ebdcd9c9469ec56","to":"implemented"},"changed":{"$aep":{"archived":false,"metadata":{"created_at":1790266492141,"id":"ent-618aae4276b6ecbd6ebdcd9c9469ec56","locator":"ep://planning/store/story/copy-linearizes-a-tree-into-sqlite","provenance":{"created_by":"human:timo","updated_by":"human:timo"},"revision":4,"type":"aep.story/v1","updated_at":1790266509545}},"status":"implemented"},"entity":"aep.entity","from_state":"active","id":"ent-618aae4276b6ecbd6ebdcd9c9469ec56","payload":{"actor":"human:timo","at":1790266509545,"causation":"cmd-child-8d2bc1c89ed729a47573d942958ece2c03d7afed4ac9ead1165d106abd9d7299","correlation":"protocol-artifact-move","event_id":"aep.entity:ent-618aae4276b6ecbd6ebdcd9c9469ec56@4#0~9c2b9c26198bcd1d","executor":null,"recorded_at":"2026-09-24T16:15:09Z"},"revision":4,"to_state":"implemented","type":"aep.status.move/v1","version":1}],"fields":{"$aep":{"archived":false,"metadata":{"created_at":1790266492141,"id":"ent-618aae4276b6ecbd6ebdcd9c9469ec56","locator":"ep://planning/store/story/copy-linearizes-a-tree-into-sqlite","provenance":{"created_by":"human:timo","updated_by":"human:timo"},"revision":4,"type":"aep.story/v1","updated_at":1790266509545}},"body":"## Outcome\n\n`eventlog_tree::copy` linearizes an `eventlog-tree` store into a SQLite store: groups in the tree's\nposition order, each stream gapless, and every event's original `{version, digest, parents}` kept\nin an origin table beside the events, so redaction cannot erase it. A refused copy writes nothing.\n\nDesign: aep `docs/design/planning-on-entity-runtime-v0.1.md` § 9.6, unit V3 (`copy`; `verify` and\n`repair` shipped in 0.4.0).\n\n## Decisions\n\n- A library function, not a CLI: this repository has no CLI crate.\n- Ori